{\b\fs28\cf1 HermiSim 2.0}\par
{\cf2 Simulation suite & IDE for TulpaLang}\par\par
{\b What gets installed}\par
\bullet  {\b HermiSim IDE} \endash  editor with Tulpa language server, run configurations, telemetry plots, VCD waveform viewer, state-machine diagrams, BOM/netlist viewer.\par
\bullet  {\b MuJoCo co-simulator} \endash  Tulpa programs drive physics through {\f1 cosim::connect()}; headless runs via {\f1 hermisim-cli}.\par
\bullet  {\b Tulpa toolchain} \endash  {\f1 tulpa} interpreter, bytecode VM, LLVM {\f1 build}, {\f1 verify}, {\f1 lsp}, plus the {\f1 std/} libraries: rtl, eda, rl, lipm, topics, frame, and native {\f1 nn::}, {\f1 pack::}, {\f1 json::}, {\f1 cosim::}.\par
\bullet  {\b Morty} \endash  bipedal humanoid sample: capture-point balance, physics-informed COM model, PPO residual policy, FPGA torque governor (RTL + behavioural), mainboard as code.\par\par
{\b Where things go}\par
Program files: the folder you choose next.  Your projects: {\f1 Documents\\HermiSim} (created on first launch).  Logs: {\f1 %LOCALAPPDATA%\\HermiSim}.\par\par
{\b Requirements}\par
Windows 10 1809 or later, 64-bit. OpenGL 3.3 capable graphics for the 3-D viewport.\par
